      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMPORTANT: `clamp()` is defined as follows:\n\n```\nstatic inline int clamp(int value, int low, int high) {\n  return value \u003c low ? low : (value \u003e high ? high : value);\n}\n```\n\nIt assumes `low \u003c\u003d high`. If `low` is greater than `high`, then `clamp` does NOT ensure that the result is \u003c\u003d `high`.\n\nSo, at this point, do we know that `-top_margin \u003c\u003d mv_limits-\u003erow_max`?",
      "revId": "9c902237e8b7be68e2d3d6aaa158aa701e0e2d8e",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
